# iOS

- Build Falcon components in SwiftUI.
- Map color, type, spacing, radius, border, and shadow to tokens in `styles/foundations.css`. Keep raw colors and point sizes out of views. Use the same names (`brand/500`, `space/4`, `radius/xl`).
- Touch targets are at least 44 pt.
- Support Dynamic Type. Give every control a VoiceOver label.
- Map icons through Falcon icon names so the same icon exists on Web and Android.

```swift
// ❌ BAD
Button("Save") { }.background(Color(red: 0, green: 0.604, blue: 0.471))

// ✅ GOOD
FalconButton("Save", variant: .primary, size: .md)
```
